Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[1,33,34]},{"id":"aaron_1","name":"Aaron","also":"","summary":"The eldest son of Amram and Jochebed, a daughter of Levi (Ex. 6:20). Some explain the name as meaning mountaineer, others mountain of strength, illuminator.","verses":331,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[1]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[2,32,33,34]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[3,9]},{"id":"amminadab_228","name":"Amminadab","also":"Aminadab","summary":"The father of Nahshon, who was chief of the tribe of Judah (Num. 1:7; 2:3; 7:12, 17; 10:14).","verses":11,"father":"Ram","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"nahshon_2144","name":"Nahshon","also":"Naasson, Naashon","summary":"Sorcerer, the son of Aminadab, and prince of the children of Judah at the time of the first numbering of the tribes in the wilderness (Ex. 6:23).","verses":11,"father":"Amminadab","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"issachar_645","name":"Issachar","also":"","summary":"Hired (Gen. 30:18). “God hath given me,” said Leah, “my hire (Heb. sekhari)...and she called his name Issachar.” He was Jacob’s ninth son, and was born in Padan-aram (comp. 28:2).","verses":38,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[5]},{"id":"nethaneel_2188","name":"Nethaneel","also":"","summary":"The son of Zuar, chief of the tribe of Issachar at the Exodus (Num. 1:8; 2:5).","verses":5,"father":"Zuar","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"zuar_3107","name":"Zuar","also":"","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"zebulun_3002","name":"Zebulun","also":"Zabulon","summary":"Dwelling, the sixth and youngest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 30:20). Little is known of his personal history.","verses":46,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[7]},{"id":"eliab_1073","name":"Eliab","also":"","summary":"A son of Helon, and chief of the tribe of Zebulun at the time of the census in the wilderness (Num. 1:9; 2:7).","verses":6,"father":"Helon","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"helon_1486","name":"Helon","also":"","summary":"Strong, father of Eliab, who was “captain of the children of Zebulun” (Num. 1:9; 2:7).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"reuben_2429","name":"Reuben","also":"","summary":"Behold a son!, the eldest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 29:32). His sinful conduct, referred to in Gen. 35:22, brought down upon him his dying father’s malediction (48:4).","verses":70,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[10,16]},{"id":"elizur_1166","name":"Elizur","also":"","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"Shedeur","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"shedeur_2591","name":"Shedeur","also":"","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"simeon_2741","name":"Simeon","also":"","summary":"The second son of Jacob by Leah (Gen. 29:33). He was associated with Levi in the terrible act of vengeance against Hamor and the Shechemites (34:25, 26).","verses":40,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[12]},{"id":"shelumiel_2612","name":"Shelumiel","also":"","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"Zurishaddai","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"zurishaddai_3113","name":"Zurishaddai","also":"","summary":"Rock of the Almighty, the father of Shelumiel, who was chief of the tribe of Simeon when Israel was encamped at Sinai (Num. 1:6; 2:12).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"gad_1262","name":"Gad","also":"","summary":"Jacob’s seventh son, by Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid, and the brother of Asher (Gen. 30:11-13; 46:16, 18).","verses":55,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[14]},{"id":"jethro_2431","name":"Jethro","also":"Deuel, Reuel, Raguel","summary":"“The priest of Midian,” Moses’ father-in-law (Ex. 2:18)=Raguel (Num. 10:29).","verses":16,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"eliasaph_1091","name":"Eliasaph","also":"","summary":"Prince of the Gershonites.","verses":5,"father":"Jethro","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[18,24]},{"id":"ammihud_223","name":"Ammihud","also":"","summary":"The father of the Ephraimite chief Elishama, at the time of the Exodus (Num. 1:10; 2:18; 7:48, 53).","verses":6,"father":"Laadan","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"elishama_1155","name":"Elishama","also":"","summary":"A prince of Benjamin, grandfather of Joshua (Num. 1:10; 1 Chr. 7:26).","verses":6,"father":"Ammihud","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"on_2247","name":"On","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"Peleth","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[20]},{"id":"gamaliel_1276","name":"Gamaliel","also":"","summary":"A chief of the tribe of Manasseh at the census at Sinai (Num. 1:10; 2:20; 7:54, 59).","verses":5,"father":"Pedahzur","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"pedahzur_2291","name":"Pedahzur","also":"","summary":"Rock of redemption, the father of Gamaliel and prince of Manasseh at the time of the Exodus (Num. 1:10; 2:20).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[22]},{"id":"abidan_22","name":"Abidan","also":"","summary":"Father of judgment; judge, head of the tribe of Benjamin at the Exodus (Num. 1:11; 2:22).","verses":5,"father":"Gideoni","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"gideoni_1315","name":"Gideoni","also":"","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[25,31]},{"id":"ahiezer_131","name":"Ahiezer","also":"","summary":"Captain of the tribe of Dan.","verses":5,"father":"Ammishaddai","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"ammishaddai_230","name":"Ammishaddai","also":"","summary":"People of the Almighty, the father of Ahiezer, who was chief of the Danites at the time of the Exodus (Num. 1:12; 2:25).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"asher_337","name":"Asher","also":"Aser","summary":"Happy, Jacob’s eigth son; his mother was Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid (Gen. 30:13). Of the tribe founded by him nothing is recorded beyond its holding a place in the list of the tribes (35:26; 46:17; Ex. 1:4, etc.) It increased in numbers twenty-nine percent, during the thirty-eight years’ wanderings.","verses":43,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[27]},{"id":"ocran_2235","name":"Ocran","also":"","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[27]},{"id":"pagiel_2264","name":"Pagiel","also":"","summary":"God allots, a prince of the tribe of Asher (Num. 1:13), in the wilderness.","verses":5,"father":"Ocran","mother":"","v":[27]},{"id":"naphtali_2149","name":"Naphtali","also":"Nephthalim","summary":"My wrestling, the fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s handmaid (Gen. 30:8). When Jacob went down into Egypt, Naphtali had four sons (Gen. 46:24).","verses":49,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[29]},{"id":"ahira_157","name":"Ahira","also":"","summary":"Brother of evil = unlucky, or my brother is f